{
  "fps": 30,
  "durationInFrames": 4113,
  "scenes": [
    {
      "id": "hook",
      "from": 0,
      "duration": 503,
      "lines": [
        {
          "text": "On one Microsoft Store launch, I surfaced four hundred craft and implementation issues in review, from line heights and spacing to loaders and dark-mode colors.",
          "file": "hook-0.wav",
          "start": 0.7,
          "seconds": 10.445041666666667,
          "from": 21,
          "duration": 313
        },
        {
          "text": "They were found by eye, after the feature was built.",
          "file": "hook-1.wav",
          "start": 11.495041666666665,
          "seconds": 2.886125,
          "from": 345,
          "duration": 87
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "title",
      "from": 503,
      "duration": 132,
      "lines": []
    },
    {
      "id": "problem",
      "from": 635,
      "duration": 479,
      "lines": [
        {
          "text": "Every issue meant the same round trip: spot the mismatch, screenshot it, write it up, file a bug, then check the fix.",
          "file": "problem-0.wav",
          "start": 21.76666666666667,
          "seconds": 7.067125,
          "from": 653,
          "duration": 212
        },
        {
          "text": "The feedback was scattered across Figma, Loop and the bug tracker, and the designer stayed the last quality gate.",
          "file": "problem-1.wav",
          "start": 29.183791666666668,
          "seconds": 6.351541666666667,
          "from": 876,
          "duration": 191
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "insight",
      "from": 1114,
      "duration": 206,
      "lines": [
        {
          "text": "Some craft decisions need a designer.",
          "file": "insight-0.wav",
          "start": 37.63333333333333,
          "seconds": 2.1952083333333334,
          "from": 1129,
          "duration": 66
        },
        {
          "text": "Most mismatches just need measuring.",
          "file": "insight-1.wav",
          "start": 40.17854166666667,
          "seconds": 2.2218333333333335,
          "from": 1205,
          "duration": 67
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "decision1",
      "from": 1320,
      "duration": 345,
      "lines": [
        {
          "text": "So I moved the check before the designer's review. Engineers drop in the design and the build, and run it.",
          "file": "decision1-0.wav",
          "start": 44.8,
          "seconds": 6.091333333333333,
          "from": 1344,
          "duration": 183
        },
        {
          "text": "There's no setup. Two screenshots are enough to start.",
          "file": "decision1-1.wav",
          "start": 51.24133333333333,
          "seconds": 3.0560416666666668,
          "from": 1537,
          "duration": 92
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "decision2",
      "from": 1665,
      "duration": 512,
      "lines": [
        {
          "text": "Each check runs two engines. First, a pixel-level color diff catches exact hex mismatches.",
          "file": "decision2-0.wav",
          "start": 56.3,
          "seconds": 6.4905,
          "from": 1689,
          "duration": 195
        },
        {
          "text": "Then an AI vision model compares both screens for copy, spacing and missing elements, the things a pixel diff can't explain.",
          "file": "decision2-1.wav",
          "start": 63.1405,
          "seconds": 8.012291666666666,
          "from": 1894,
          "duration": 240
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "decision3",
      "from": 2177,
      "duration": 432,
      "lines": [
        {
          "text": "Every issue names the property, the design value, and the built value.",
          "file": "decision3-0.wav",
          "start": 73.36666666666666,
          "seconds": 4.1415,
          "from": 2201,
          "duration": 124
        },
        {
          "text": "Hover an issue, and its region lights up on the build. Filters let designers and engineers each focus on what matters to them.",
          "file": "decision3-1.wav",
          "start": 77.85816666666666,
          "seconds": 7.710166666666667,
          "from": 2336,
          "duration": 231
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "decision4",
      "from": 2609,
      "duration": 338,
      "lines": [
        {
          "text": "Then it goes straight into the team's workflow.",
          "file": "decision4-0.wav",
          "start": 87.76666666666667,
          "seconds": 2.0597083333333335,
          "from": 2633,
          "duration": 62
        },
        {
          "text": "One click files a pre-filled bug in Azure DevOps, or copies every issue into Loop as a ready table.",
          "file": "decision4-1.wav",
          "start": 90.17637500000001,
          "seconds": 6.652791666666666,
          "from": 2705,
          "duration": 200
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "result",
      "from": 2947,
      "duration": 836,
      "lines": [
        {
          "text": "I built Craft Check on my own with AI: a React app with Fluent UI, a server, and a command line tool that also compares Figma tokens with CSS and Windows XAML.",
          "file": "result-0.wav",
          "start": 99.03333333333333,
          "seconds": 11.523458333333334,
          "from": 2971,
          "duration": 346
        },
        {
          "text": "It's a working prototype, which I took to Microsoft's F H L hackathon in March twenty twenty-six. Next, direct Figma integration, then running the check automatically before code is merged.",
          "file": "result-1.wav",
          "start": 110.90679166666666,
          "seconds": 12.807,
          "from": 3327,
          "duration": 384
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "takeaway",
      "from": 3783,
      "duration": 180,
      "lines": [
        {
          "text": "Automate the measuring, so designers can spend their time on judgment.",
          "file": "takeaway-0.wav",
          "start": 126.6,
          "seconds": 4.087625,
          "from": 3798,
          "duration": 123
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "end",
      "from": 3963,
      "duration": 150,
      "lines": []
    }
  ]
}
